WEBVTT

00:15.110 --> 00:20.040
The place where the dark swallowed all that
crossed its path and took everything from us...

00:21.750 --> 00:24.210
...has become known as the Lightless Realm.

00:25.420 --> 00:27.250
And from there,

00:27.250 --> 00:34.130
were born aberrations that seemed to be perfect reflections of human's despair and chaos.

00:37.050 --> 00:38.970
They were called...

00:40.390 --> 00:41.810
Admonitions.

00:46.270 --> 00:49.820
Hey, where are you?

00:52.780 --> 00:54.780
Hey!

00:55.700 --> 00:58.370
Where is everyone?

00:59.410 --> 01:01.330
Where?

01:04.040 --> 01:06.210
Over here!

01:06.710 --> 01:08.750
I'm right over here!

01:16.340 --> 01:16.970
What?

01:16.970 --> 01:17.510
What is this?

01:17.510 --> 01:18.720
Something's coming!

01:18.720 --> 01:19.970
I'm scared!

01:19.970 --> 01:20.850
Don't.

01:42.120 --> 01:47.710
The Dark Metal

01:42.120 --> 01:42.160
The Dark Metal

01:47.710 --> 01:52.130
Night turns to day, and day turns to night. Our wishes have wilted away

01:52.130 --> 01:56.300
Where did the person I want to meet go?

01:56.300 --> 02:00.760
Interlocking these fingers with my beloved

02:00.760 --> 02:04.520
Even though I can't feel them, I continue to live

02:04.560 --> 02:09.150
When the flower's petals

02:09.150 --> 02:13.270
Are plucked off by the wind's playful gale

02:13.270 --> 02:17.740
They are scattered in every direction

02:17.740 --> 02:23.080
Even if you long for it

02:24.080 --> 02:28.790
Do it without disappearing

02:28.790 --> 02:32.590
I can even give everything else away if I have to

02:32.590 --> 02:37.420
You were there, and I was there with you

02:37.420 --> 02:41.760
Let me take in these memories

02:41.760 --> 02:48.680
These brief moments are connected, turning it into eternity

03:06.910 --> 03:11.960
Episode 1
Starry Night

03:11.540 --> 03:13.170
Thank you very much!

03:15.800 --> 03:15.840
Kawadahara Kujujicho Store

03:17.880 --> 03:19.670
It is now 7 o'clock.

03:19.670 --> 03:22.300
It is dangerous to wander out at night.

03:22.930 --> 03:25.760
Please return home immediately.

03:25.760 --> 03:29.600
If you happen to witness something abnormal,

03:29.600 --> 03:35.230
please report it to the nearest police
station or an IX public safety security office.

04:11.770 --> 04:14.810
Hey, aren't students supposed to be home by now?

04:14.810 --> 04:16.480
That was my chance!

04:16.770 --> 04:18.900
Oh, I'm sorry.

04:19.900 --> 04:21.110
Damn that red poop!

04:21.110 --> 04:22.700
Red poop?

04:26.160 --> 04:29.290
I didn't think there'd be any people at this hour.

04:29.290 --> 04:33.370
We're obligated to confirm civilian presence before firing, right?

04:33.370 --> 04:35.120
Of course I know that!

04:35.580 --> 04:39.130
Your license and IX company badge please...

04:35.880 --> 04:41.670
Inquiry for Raika Kasumi, piloting Vess Tower type T1.

04:40.250 --> 04:42.090
Jeez, fine.

04:41.670 --> 04:43.800
Yes. Yes. Please do.

04:42.090 --> 04:43.800
Here's my license!

04:43.800 --> 04:45.340
And sign here.

04:45.340 --> 04:48.550
I totally won't catch that red poop now!

04:48.550 --> 04:49.600
Red poop?

04:49.600 --> 04:50.260
What's that?

04:50.260 --> 04:50.640
Excuse me...

04:50.640 --> 04:54.310
Red poop is red poop!
That Admonition that ran by before!

04:54.310 --> 04:56.400
I don't care anymore! Just hurry it up!

04:58.860 --> 05:03.070
Kawadahara City, home of
reconstruction support enterprise IX.

05:03.400 --> 05:08.990
Within the city are various companies and facilities operated by IX.

05:09.450 --> 05:13.870
And this school, known as
Kukunochi Academy, is one of them.

05:14.370 --> 05:16.620
I heard this last one was pretty huge.

05:16.620 --> 05:17.710
Really?

05:17.710 --> 05:21.300
I thought Admonitions were the size of a boar or something like that?

05:21.300 --> 05:24.090
So that big one got hunted down...

05:24.090 --> 05:26.630
Bad news... It got away.

05:26.630 --> 05:27.930
That's not good.

05:28.430 --> 05:33.270
Students, who've grown used to a life
seeking refuge from the Lightless Realm,

05:33.270 --> 05:36.640
have gotten so acclimated to this abnormal life

05:36.640 --> 05:40.270
that the Admonition threat can
become but a mere subject of gossip.

05:40.770 --> 05:41.940
You're kidding!

05:41.940 --> 05:44.190
My friend's dad said it too.

05:44.940 --> 05:49.120
And they don't even know that they are the next target...

05:52.410 --> 05:55.500
And you know what? They saw a Corpse.

05:56.160 --> 06:00.080
They say when Corpses show up, you can hear a song.

06:00.080 --> 06:02.550
Doesn't that rumor sound like it's made up?

06:03.250 --> 06:04.340
A Corpse...

06:04.960 --> 06:09.340
A mysterious being said to be the Lightless Realm's guardian...

06:09.510 --> 06:18.980
Corpse Song 9 Days Mysterious Death
Mysteriously Within the Next 9

06:09.890 --> 06:14.770
Those who hear the Corpse's Song die mysteriously within the next nine days.

06:18.980 --> 06:22.940
Restroom Being Cleaned

06:19.650 --> 06:22.940
These Admonitions and Corpses are such a pain.

06:22.940 --> 06:24.280
Like, really.

06:24.280 --> 06:26.740
Oh, lend me your blush.

06:26.740 --> 06:30.360
Plastering that on won't make you any less ugly.

06:30.700 --> 06:33.240
You say something, old hag?

06:33.240 --> 06:35.700
It stinks so bad I couldn't hear you.

06:35.700 --> 06:37.960
Saginuma-senpai!

06:37.960 --> 06:39.170
Akashi-kun?

06:39.170 --> 06:41.080
Looks like he's in a match.

06:43.250 --> 06:44.840
Who's he fighting?

06:44.840 --> 06:46.550
Probably Iwato-kun.

06:55.810 --> 06:57.180
Saginuma-senpai!

06:57.180 --> 06:59.100
Nothing less from him!

06:59.100 --> 07:03.020
By the way, you hear about the special course they're making?

07:03.020 --> 07:06.030
You mean the one that'll teach us how to fight Admonitions and Corpses one day?

07:06.030 --> 07:07.230
I have heard!

07:07.230 --> 07:09.400
They chose Akashi-kun, right?

07:09.400 --> 07:12.490
Really? Well, I guess that makes sense.

07:37.600 --> 07:39.810
Can't you go a little easier on me?

07:41.440 --> 07:44.480
There's not much of a gap in skill between us.

07:45.310 --> 07:47.230
This kinda irritates me...

07:47.820 --> 07:50.240
Akashi-kun!

07:51.200 --> 07:54.070
Well, it's truly an honorable thing.

07:54.530 --> 07:57.740
To think three of our students were chosen.

07:57.740 --> 08:00.830
Akashi I get, but why me too?

08:00.830 --> 08:03.620
I'm happy I'm going with a friend!

08:03.620 --> 08:05.920
There was like zero heart in that.

08:07.500 --> 08:10.380
It looks like luck is finally turning my way.

08:10.380 --> 08:13.010
I don't know why I was chosen,

08:13.010 --> 08:17.850
but I have to make use of this chance I was given to start a brand new life!

08:20.270 --> 08:23.600
Excuse me! I'm getting on!

08:25.310 --> 08:26.650
I'm so sorry!

08:26.650 --> 08:27.570
No problem...

08:30.740 --> 08:33.570
This is a really pretty building.

08:33.570 --> 08:36.370
I've never been in the IX building before!

08:36.370 --> 08:37.660
How about you, Akashi-kun?

08:38.530 --> 08:40.700
How do you know my name?

08:41.700 --> 08:43.370
Come to think of it, it's pretty weird!

08:44.210 --> 08:46.290
Why do you think I know?

08:46.290 --> 08:47.420
No clue.

08:49.170 --> 08:50.630
Red poop...

08:56.510 --> 08:59.970
And those are the basics of this training course.

08:56.510 --> 08:56.550
Lightless Realm Investigation Team

08:56.510 --> 08:56.550
Inaugural Special Investigation Team

08:56.510 --> 08:56.550
Pilot Training Course

08:56.510 --> 08:56.550
Briefing Site

09:01.970 --> 09:07.230
which means IX is officially in charge of
the investigation in the Lightless Realm.

09:08.060 --> 09:12.190
You're honorable members of the inaugural class of this team.

09:12.190 --> 09:13.690
I have high hopes.

09:13.690 --> 09:17.450
Excuse me, but we didn't volunteer for this...

09:17.450 --> 09:22.660
There is no problem.

09:22.660 --> 09:24.040
Our lab team investigated thoroughly for aptitude before deciding on you.

09:24.040 --> 09:27.040
No... That's not what we mean.

09:27.040 --> 09:32.420
Second years from Kukonochi Academy, Akashi Saginuma and Iwato Namito.

09:32.420 --> 09:33.420
Yeah...

09:33.420 --> 09:36.550
From the same school, first year Mahmu Yuzuki.

09:36.550 --> 09:37.300
Um...

09:37.300 --> 09:40.010
Temp worker, Emiru Hazaki.

09:40.010 --> 09:43.600
Vess test pilot, Raika Kasumi.

09:45.020 --> 09:45.060
HEITO ISAKU

09:45.020 --> 09:45.060
SASAME IZURI

09:45.020 --> 09:45.060
MINASHI MAKI

09:45.140 --> 09:48.400
And three more who were not able to make it here.

09:48.400 --> 09:50.820
That is your team.

09:51.730 --> 09:53.030
Any questions?

09:53.030 --> 09:56.950
Can we enter the Lightless Realm and come back alive?

09:56.950 --> 09:59.660
That's what the new Vess model's for.

09:59.660 --> 10:04.950
Besides, if the Lightless Realm continues to expand, everything will eventually be within it.

10:05.250 --> 10:07.620
What a pointless question to ask.

10:10.380 --> 10:13.300
Oh, the dorms are ready too.

10:13.300 --> 10:15.090
You can move in tomorrow.

10:15.670 --> 10:18.130
If you have no more questions, disperse.

10:22.350 --> 10:25.890
But in any case, this is a pretty dull room.

10:26.140 --> 10:29.520
I came to help you move out, but I have nothing to do.

10:30.440 --> 10:31.730
Let's have some cake.

10:32.060 --> 10:34.690
I'll come by to clean this room every so often.

10:35.860 --> 10:37.740
You're not taking any dishes?

10:37.740 --> 10:39.450
They said the dorm has stuff like that.

10:40.110 --> 10:41.530
Of course.

10:42.700 --> 10:47.370
Kasane-san, you knew about the
pilot course for a while now, didn't you?

10:48.750 --> 10:51.670
There's this thing called a nondisclosure agreement.

10:51.670 --> 10:54.000
It's hard being an adult.

10:55.170 --> 10:58.260
Hey, take a look inside my bag.

11:07.060 --> 11:10.770
I thought I had deleted the data, but I found it.

11:10.770 --> 11:13.270
It's back from Aoshi's award ceremony.

11:13.770 --> 11:15.980
Aoshi had such an amazing smile.

11:15.980 --> 11:18.320
Though you had a sulky look.

11:19.490 --> 11:20.400
It's yours.

11:21.070 --> 11:23.530
I'm not really interested in photographs.

11:26.740 --> 11:27.950
Where are you going?

11:27.950 --> 11:29.120
To throw out the trash.

11:30.330 --> 11:32.460
Why don't you have some cake first?

11:32.460 --> 11:35.460
It's your favorite, peach shortcake!

11:35.460 --> 11:36.920
Wait...

11:36.920 --> 11:39.800
Stop treating me like a child.

11:39.800 --> 11:42.840
You came all the way to a guy's room by yourself.

11:42.840 --> 11:45.800
Are you sexually frustrated or something?

11:49.640 --> 11:52.440
What's with that? Is he going through a rebellious period?

12:10.660 --> 12:11.710
What's that?

12:21.340 --> 12:22.420
A song?

12:49.740 --> 12:51.910
An accident during an investigation...

12:52.540 --> 12:55.210
And Akashi is still so young.

12:55.210 --> 12:56.420
What a pity...

12:58.130 --> 13:00.960
I'll protect Akashi from now on.

13:01.380 --> 13:02.760
Why...

13:02.760 --> 13:05.010
From now on, I'll...

13:05.720 --> 13:07.140
Why is it?

13:08.390 --> 13:11.140
You're the one who deserves to die the most.

13:12.640 --> 13:14.020
It's you, yet...

13:15.100 --> 13:15.560
Lightless Realm Investigation

13:15.100 --> 13:15.560
Aoshi Saginuma (Age 19) Passes Test

13:28.910 --> 13:30.080
Akashi!

13:30.080 --> 13:30.910
Yeah?

13:31.990 --> 13:34.410
That's all you're moving in with?

13:34.410 --> 13:35.500
Yeah, why?

13:35.500 --> 13:37.040
You barely have anything.

13:37.920 --> 13:39.040
They're here!

13:39.590 --> 13:42.760
Oh, hey, my buddies!

13:42.760 --> 13:45.010
It's... Hazaki?

13:45.010 --> 13:47.380
Wow, you remember me?

13:47.380 --> 13:49.140
I'm Emiru Hazaki.

13:49.140 --> 13:52.060
Nice to meet you again, Akashi-kun.

13:53.810 --> 13:55.270
What's this?

13:57.060 --> 13:59.020
Oh, I picked that up somewhere...

13:59.020 --> 14:01.770
No way, it's so cute!

14:01.770 --> 14:03.280
If you don't want it, can I have it?

14:03.280 --> 14:05.610
I guess you can...

14:06.990 --> 14:08.610
I wonder if people will be suspicious...

14:10.370 --> 14:12.530
Well? Does it look good?

14:13.040 --> 14:16.210
Is she painfully lacking in common sense?

14:16.210 --> 14:17.330
Yeah.

14:17.830 --> 14:21.210
I was already working as a test pilot,

14:21.210 --> 14:26.090
so why do I have to go to school again?

14:26.090 --> 14:30.260
Um, Raika-san, can I ask you a question?

14:30.930 --> 14:32.350
Mahmu, right?

14:32.350 --> 14:33.010
What's up?

14:33.350 --> 14:38.810
I heard that Admonitions are ghosts of the
people who've died within the Lightless Realm.

14:38.810 --> 14:41.730
Well, I wouldn't necessarily say ghosts...

14:42.820 --> 14:48.700
Human muscle tissue has been extracted from captured Admonitions in the past.

14:49.530 --> 14:52.620
So the theory is that the metallic crystals

14:52.620 --> 14:56.370
in the Lightless Realm assimilate dead
humans and turn them into Admonitions.

14:57.500 --> 15:01.080
Well, I guess you could call them ghosts, after all.

15:05.880 --> 15:09.930
I've been wanting to head into the
Lightless Realm for some time now.

15:10.300 --> 15:11.640
Right...

15:11.640 --> 15:13.550
Because that's where your big brother...

15:15.100 --> 15:19.770
But still, suddenly being told that we'll be trained to become pilots...

15:19.770 --> 15:24.770
The friends we've yet to meet were
Minashi-kun, Heito-kun, and Sasame-chan, right?

15:25.270 --> 15:28.070
I have high hopes for Sasame-chan!

15:28.070 --> 15:31.570
And I sure hope the classes won't be needlessly tough.

15:33.990 --> 15:35.870
That hurts...

15:37.290 --> 15:38.540
What is this?

15:38.540 --> 15:40.580
Training for your reflexes.

15:44.080 --> 15:46.750
It's still too early to give up!

15:48.550 --> 15:49.920
Just die...

15:51.930 --> 15:54.050
This looks real.

15:54.050 --> 15:57.810
Wait, this is so fun! Let's go!

15:58.180 --> 16:01.810
Stop! I'm telling you to stop!

16:01.810 --> 16:05.310
Admonitions are clusters of metallic crystals.

16:05.310 --> 16:07.860
So even if you attack them,
they immediately repair themselves.

16:07.860 --> 16:12.990
Thus, in order to defeat them, it is necessary to strongly thrust a special stake into their vitals with the penetrator.

16:12.990 --> 16:18.490
By the way, these stakes are 20 million yen each, so don't waste any of them!

16:19.540 --> 16:21.910
Why are you all asleep?!

16:21.910 --> 16:24.290
It's been too exhausting, each and every day.

16:24.290 --> 16:25.420
Excuses are evil!

16:25.670 --> 16:30.710
Starting from 20:00 hours today, I'll be doubling your training by adding outside patrol in the residential quarters.

16:30.710 --> 16:34.970
On the Vesses today are Akashi Saginuma and Emiru Hazaki.

16:34.970 --> 16:37.300
Oh, me? No way!

16:37.300 --> 16:40.930
Wait. There's a chance we'll encounter an Admonition.

16:41.350 --> 16:45.270
From past data, it's a region low in appearances.

16:45.270 --> 16:47.650
But that red poop... I mean,

16:47.650 --> 16:51.900
the Admonition I let escape hasn't been caught yet.

16:51.900 --> 16:53.860
I should be going today.

16:53.860 --> 16:56.870
I've fought Admonitions as a test pilot...

16:57.240 --> 17:00.370
This is training! Not a place to show off!

17:00.370 --> 17:01.120
But still!

17:01.120 --> 17:04.370
Don't make me say it again! This is training!

17:04.370 --> 17:06.960
Damn, I can't make myself any more clearer to this girl!

17:09.880 --> 17:13.670
Hey, teach me all sorts of stuff.

17:13.670 --> 17:14.720
Sure.

17:31.070 --> 17:35.280
The technology to reliably detect
Admonitions has yet to be completed.

17:35.280 --> 17:37.490
In other words, we won't know until they show up?

17:37.490 --> 17:39.830
You can rely on your instinct!

17:45.790 --> 17:46.670
What?

17:46.670 --> 17:48.500
I saw a response just now...

17:48.500 --> 17:49.790
Was it an Admonition?

17:50.380 --> 17:54.050
I've already told you that this region in the past—

17:56.220 --> 17:57.680
You're kidding!

18:03.560 --> 18:05.140
That's...

18:06.640 --> 18:08.020
Red poop!

18:08.020 --> 18:09.650
Akashi! Protect Emiru!

18:09.650 --> 18:10.900
Already on it!

18:11.980 --> 18:14.230
N-No!

18:15.990 --> 18:18.110
Go away!

18:19.160 --> 18:21.870
Twenty... million... yen...

18:26.080 --> 18:27.960
No!

18:33.460 --> 18:34.920
Dammit!

18:34.920 --> 18:36.210
That thing...

18:36.210 --> 18:38.050
It's only going after Emiru.

18:38.050 --> 18:39.760
But why?

18:45.720 --> 18:47.430
That's an Admonition?

18:48.440 --> 18:49.310
Huh?

18:50.350 --> 18:51.650
It's an IX Vess!

18:51.650 --> 18:53.150
A civilian?

18:53.150 --> 18:56.150
Wait... I think that's Minashi Maki...

19:03.780 --> 19:05.660
I've had enough!

19:25.140 --> 19:27.140
Is she all right?

19:27.140 --> 19:28.560
Right here.

19:31.310 --> 19:32.520
Where?

19:32.520 --> 19:33.980
Right here.

19:33.980 --> 19:35.570
Where?

19:35.570 --> 19:36.940
It's all right...

19:36.940 --> 19:39.280
Where is everyone?

19:39.280 --> 19:40.530
Right here.

19:43.820 --> 19:44.990
Just now...

19:44.990 --> 19:46.280
Here?

19:46.280 --> 19:47.870
You heard that too?

19:48.450 --> 19:50.370
Heard what?

19:50.710 --> 19:52.790
What was that just now?

19:55.340 --> 19:56.040
Hold on...

19:59.840 --> 20:01.010
This one too...

20:01.510 --> 20:03.590
This one's searching too.

20:03.590 --> 20:05.050
Searching?

20:09.980 --> 20:12.980
Emiru! Throw me the pendant I gave you earlier!

20:12.980 --> 20:15.400
I'm in no condition to do so!

20:15.400 --> 20:16.690
I can't even stand up.

20:16.690 --> 20:18.940
Why don't you knock this thing out!

20:18.940 --> 20:20.860
Hurry up, pig girl!

20:20.860 --> 20:22.450
P-Pig?

20:22.450 --> 20:25.120
What part of me is a pig!

20:25.120 --> 20:28.200
Fine. Take it back, you impotent jerk!

20:39.340 --> 20:40.590
This is...

20:40.590 --> 20:42.840
It reacted to the pendant?

20:43.260 --> 20:47.510
That Admonition is probably a mother that lost her child...

20:48.510 --> 20:52.020
When you say that, it makes it harder for us to defeat it.

21:01.070 --> 21:04.280
This thing is trapped by its past...

21:04.280 --> 21:05.280
Akashi?

21:05.280 --> 21:06.280
Hey...

21:08.370 --> 21:14.160
Getting killed is less painful
than being trapped by your past.

21:14.960 --> 21:18.710
So much easier than being trapped by the past...

21:42.860 --> 21:44.440
Akashi...

21:54.040 --> 21:55.410
A song?

22:01.040 --> 22:02.250
That's...

22:02.880 --> 22:04.710
...a Corpse.

22:27.570 --> 22:33.450
On a starry night, they heard the Corpse's song.

22:44.710 --> 22:55.350
Throwing away all my excuses, I traced over my abrased heart

22:55.350 --> 22:59.890
In the coldness of the locker room,

22:59.890 --> 23:06.360
Was an unfulfilled promise, locked away

23:06.860 --> 23:12.820
Dispel the darkness in this fallen world,

23:12.820 --> 23:17.370
And give me a reason why I should continue living

23:17.370 --> 23:22.750
The meaning of good-byes, the expectations of people,

23:22.750 --> 23:27.630
And the melodies that we played while never crossing paths

23:27.630 --> 23:33.350
I know I must not run away. The only path is straight ahead

23:33.350 --> 23:37.850
Even if this turns out to be a mistake

23:37.850 --> 23:43.440
The whirlpools of destiny will consume all loneliness

23:43.440 --> 23:51.530
It is an unerasable scar, an egoism that cannot be discarded

24:05.000 --> 24:10.010
Episode 2

24:05.000 --> 24:10.010
Embraced by the Reaper
